WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:13.251
I stared at Josh.

2
00:00:13.252 --> 00:00:18.205
Bunch was gone—really gone?

3
00:00:18.206 --> 00:00:21.628
Josh, Jenny, Molly, and I hurried outside.

4
00:00:21.629 --> 00:00:23.900
Caswell followed us.

5
00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:28.261
"I don't understand what's wrong," said Molly.

6
00:00:28.262 --> 00:00:31.651
"Wasn't Bunch supposed to disappear?"

7
00:00:31.652 --> 00:00:36.238
"Yes, but Bunch truly disappeared," Josh told her.

8
00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:38.567
"Even my dad doesn't know where he is.

9
00:00:38.568 --> 00:00:40.862
We've got to find him fast."

10
00:00:40.863 --> 00:00:43.427
Jenny was about to cry.

11
00:00:43.428 --> 00:00:47.907
"Poor Bunch! He could be lost!"

12
00:00:47.908 --> 00:00:51.811
"I wonder how he got out of the box," I said.

13
00:00:51.812 --> 00:00:56.429
"I didn't mean to do it!" cried Caswell.

14
00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:58.797
We all stared at him.

15
00:00:58.798 --> 00:01:01.579
"Caswell!" said Molly.

16
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.477
"What did you do?"

17
00:01:04.478 --> 00:01:11.020
"I opened the box when I was under the table," said Caswell, hanging his head.

18
00:01:11.021 --> 00:01:15.180
"I wanted to see how Bunch disappeared."

19
00:01:15.181 --> 00:01:18.923
"So that's how Bunch escaped," I said.

20
00:01:18.924 --> 00:01:21.473
"But where is he now?"

21
00:01:21.474 --> 00:01:23.841
Caswell looked worried.

22
00:01:23.842 --> 00:01:30.417
"I hope Bunch doesn't get stranded in the mountains."

23
00:01:30.418 --> 00:01:35.905
"Too bad he didn't have any rainbow trail pellets, Iggy," said Molly.

24
00:01:35.906 --> 00:01:38.989
"Then we could follow his pellet trail."

25
00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:41.132
I glanced at the ground.

26
00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:46.139
Luckily, most of the pellets that had spilled out earlier were still there.

27
00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:48.985
Then I noticed something.

28
00:01:48.986 --> 00:01:51.325
"Look, guys!" I said.

29
00:01:51.326 --> 00:01:56.810
"Only the red pellets are left."

30
00:01:56.811 --> 00:02:01.781
"What happened to all the other colors?" asked Molly.

31
00:02:01.782 --> 00:02:06.922
"Bunch ate them!" I cried. "Except for all the red ones.

32
00:02:06.923 --> 00:02:11.113
Bunch doesn't like red. Remember?"

33
00:02:11.114 --> 00:02:16.658
"Maybe the trail of red pellets will lead to Bunch!" said Jenny.

34
00:02:16.659 --> 00:02:20.116
"I'll go tell my dad!" said Josh.

35
00:02:20.117 --> 00:02:23.563
"Wait!" I said. "I have an idea.

36
00:02:23.564 --> 00:02:25.827
The audience can help look for Bunch.

37
00:02:25.828 --> 00:02:29.247
Finding Bunch can be part of the magic trick."

38
00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:34.005
"Awesome idea, Iggy," said Josh.

39
00:02:34.006 --> 00:02:40.772
Inside, Mr. Chen was finishing his string trick.

40
00:02:40.773 --> 00:02:44.359
Josh rushed up and whispered to him.

41
00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:48.213
Mr. Chen nodded and then turned back to the crowd.

42
00:02:48.214 --> 00:02:53.201
"We will now return to the vanishing dog trick," he announced.

43
00:02:53.202 --> 00:02:55.831
"For this, I have a special surprise.

44
00:02:55.832 --> 00:02:58.824
Everyone, please follow me outside."

45
00:02:58.825 --> 00:03:04.024
The audience followed Mr. Chen outside.

46
00:03:04.025 --> 00:03:08.689
Mr. Scary trailed along, frowning.

47
00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:13.058
"This is a very unusual trick," he muttered.

48
00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:17.106
"Are you absolutely sure it will work?"

49
00:03:17.107 --> 00:03:23.233
I could see a little doubt in Mr. Chen's eyes too, but he nodded at Mr. Scary.

50
00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:28.752
"Find the trail of red, and it will lead to the dog!" he called to the audience.

51
00:03:28.753 --> 00:03:32.115
"Now let's all say the magic words."

52
00:03:32.116 --> 00:03:35.264
"Abracadabra, click and clack.

53
00:03:35.265 --> 00:03:44.644
Bring that little dog right back!" said the audience.

54
00:03:44.645 --> 00:03:50.220
Everyone followed the trail of red pellets up to the tower.

55
00:03:50.221 --> 00:03:55.319
"I see him! There's the doggie!" cried Brandy.

56
00:03:55.320 --> 00:04:03.350
Sure enough, there was Bunch, sitting near the tower, licking his lips.

57
00:04:03.351 --> 00:04:08.109
"What a great trick!" cried the lady in the blue hat.

58
00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:13.465
"Hmm . . . that was quite a trick," said Mr. Scary.

59
00:04:13.466 --> 00:04:17.103
"How did you do it?" he asked Mr. Chen.

60
00:04:17.104 --> 00:04:24.230
Mr. Chen smiled. "A magician never reveals his secrets."

61
00:04:24.231 --> 00:04:30.978
After that everyone trooped back down to the Lake Lounge for lemonade and cookies.

62
00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:36.117
"Iggy's special pellet invention saved the day," said Josh.

63
00:04:36.118 --> 00:04:39.549
"It certainly did," said Mr. Chen.

64
00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:43.566
"That was a very fine invention, Iggy."

65
00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:50.466
"But, Caswell," said Molly, "don't ever interfere with Mr. Chen's magic show again."

66
00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:56.131
"I won't," promised Caswell, grabbing another cookie.

67
00:04:56.132 --> 00:05:02.847
"I wonder why Mr. Scary keeps staring at my dad?" said Josh in a low voice.

68
00:05:02.848 --> 00:05:06.541
"He looks like he has something up his sleeve," I said.

69
00:05:06.542 --> 00:05:11.272
"Does he have a gold coin up his sleeve?" asked Caswell.

70
00:05:11.273 --> 00:05:13.969
"Is he going to do a magic trick?"

71
00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:16.851
"No, Caswell," Molly said.

72
00:05:16.852 --> 00:05:20.897
"Iggy just means that Mr. Scary is plotting something."

73
00:05:20.898 --> 00:05:24.364
"Maybe it's something good," said Josh.

74
00:05:24.365 --> 00:05:26.130
I didn't say anything.

75
00:05:26.131 --> 00:05:29.501
But I was watching Mr. Scary closely.

76
00:05:29.502 --> 00:05:36.930
And I didn't think he was plotting anything good.
